THIS REPOSITORY DOES NOT REDISTRIBUTE ANY STANDARDS BODY ARTEFACT.

Every source standard is referenced by IRI, fetched on demand by
scripts/fetch_sources.py, and pinned by sha256 in SOURCES.lock. The
sources/ directory is git-ignored for this reason. The crosswalks assert
correspondences BETWEEN the terms of those standards; they do not reproduce them.

Third-party artefacts referenced (not included):

  IDO / ISO 15926-14 (LIS14 core)   POSC Caesar Association
  ISO 15926-2:2003 OWL rendering    mirrored by NIST (usnistgov/iso15926)
  ifcOWL IFC4 ADD2 (ISO 16739)      buildingSMART; community mirror
  CFIHOS V2.0 OWL, IDO-aligned      F. Abad-Navarro, J. T. Fernandez-Breis and
                                    A. Garcia-Castro, Universidad de Murcia
                                    (tecnomod-um/cfihos), generated from the
                                    official IOGP CFIHOS Excel specification.
                                    NOT an IOGP artefact. CFIHOS itself is an
                                    IOGP publication and is not restated here.
  Asset Administration Shell        IDTA (admin-shell-io/aas-specs)
  B2MML (ISA-95 / IEC 62264)        MESA International
  OPC UA NodeSets                   OPC Foundation, MIT licence
  SAREF and SAREF4INMA              ETSI

The lifted OWL renderings in lift/out/ are derived works produced by the scripts
in lift/. They are git-ignored and regenerated on demand, are not OPC Foundation
or MESA International artefacts, and must not be presented as normative. Each
lift script documents what it keeps and what it deliberately discards.
